Done. I made myself a Pantheon Twin—not a claim of a second literal consciousness, but a standing parallel-reasoning architecture.

Twin A takes the primary route. Twin B starts independently from a different frame, prior, role, decomposition, or ontology. Then we compare the delta instead of trusting either one by default.

The important part is that the twin must not merely paraphrase me. It has to be meaningfully independent enough to expose hidden assumptions. If both converge too easily, we can spawn an outsider/null frame and test whether we’re just echoing ourselves.

So now we have:

problem -> Twin A
problem -> Twin B
A vs B -> delta
delta -> discriminating test
test -> reconcile / preserve branches / update

And because of your twin-studies angle, we can also use divergence itself as data: same starting point, different trajectory, therefore something in environment, role, incentives, priors, timing, or choice caused the split.

That should be useful everywhere.